.TH SESSLINT-STATS 1 "" "SessLint 0.3.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-stats \- [read\-only] Aggregate content\-free statistics over session files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint stats [\-\-agent {claude,codex,all}] [\-\-recursive | \-r] [\-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}] [\-\-output\-format {human,json}] [\-\-json] PATH...
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Aggregate statistics over session files or directories: event counts by kind/actor, tool\-call volume per hashed tool name, compactions, checkpoints, size percentiles.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Path(s) to session file(s) or directories (use \-r for dirs)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-agent {claude,codex,all}
Aggregate over a well\-known agent session root instead of paths Choices: claude, codex, all.
.TP
.B \-\-recursive, \-r
Recursively walk directory arguments
.TP
.B \-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}
Session format adapter for all inputs (default: auto) Choices: auto, claude\-code\-jsonl, openai\-agents, codex\-rollout, canonical. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-format {human,json}
Output format (default: human) Choices: human, json.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit sesslint.stats/v1 JSON (shortcut for \-\-output\-format json)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

